jobs.description:
The Vice President of Operational Excellence is responsible for developing and driving an enterprise-wide operational excellence strategy. Through process optimization, performance management, continuous improvement, digital transformation, and cross-functional collaboration, this role enhances the organization’s overall operational efficiency, management quality, and execution capability. Typically spanning multiple business units, the position focuses on identifying operational bottlenecks, establishing standardized management systems, spearheading operational improvement initiatives, and scaling successful practices across the entire enterprise.

Core Responsibilities

I. Operational Excellence Strategy
- Develop the enterprise’s operational excellence strategy and long-term development roadmap.
- Translate corporate strategic goals into specific objectives for operational efficiency, quality, and productivity.
- Establish an enterprise-wide framework for continuous improvement and operational management standards.
- Define operational KPIs, performance targets, and improvement priorities.
- Embed the philosophy of operational excellence across all business units.

II. Business Process Optimization
- Conduct comprehensive assessments of core business processes to identify efficiency bottlenecks and resource waste.
- Drive the standardization, simplification, and automation of business processes.
- Establish end-to-end process management mechanisms.
- Optimize cross-departmental workflows and collaboration models.
- Continuously shorten business cycle times and enhance overall execution efficiency.

III. Continuous Improvement and Quality Management
- Build an enterprise-wide continuous improvement management system.
- Lead initiatives such as Lean, Six Sigma, and Kaizen.
- Promote root-cause analysis, problem-solving, and quality enhancement.
- Identify improvement opportunities based on operational data and develop implementation plans.
- Scale successful improvement practices across various business units.

IV. Operational Performance Management
- Establish an enterprise-level operational performance management system.
- Design KPIs, OKRs, and operational performance dashboards.
- Periodically evaluate the operational performance of individual business units.
- Identify performance gaps and drive the implementation of corrective or improvement measures.
- Regularly report operational outcomes to the CEO, COO, and senior leadership.

V. Digital and Automation Transformation
- Drive the digitalization and intelligent transformation of core operational processes;
- Evaluate the application of AI, automation, and data analytics tools in operational management;
- Collaborate with the CIO, CTO, and technical teams to implement digital improvement initiatives;
- Establish data-driven decision-making mechanisms for operations;
- Facilitate the adoption of digital operational standards and best practices.

VI. Cost and Resource Efficiency Management
- Analyze the company’s operational cost structure and resource utilization;
- Identify opportunities for cost optimization, productivity enhancement, and resource integration;
- Optimize the allocation of human, technical, and business resources;
- Promote the implementation of replicable and scalable operational management models;
- Improve overall corporate resource utilization and operational returns.

VII. Organizational Collaboration and Change Management
- Collaborate with departments including Operations, Finance, Sales, Marketing, Product, and Technology;
- Lead cross-functional operational improvement and corporate transformation initiatives;
- Drive changes in organizational processes, management systems, and operational models;
- Establish mechanisms for change communication, execution, and impact assessment;
- Ensure that improvement outcomes are sustained and continuously optimized over the long term.

VIII. Team Building and Talent Development
- Build and manage an enterprise-level Operational Excellence team;
- Manage personnel such as Senior Directors, Directors, and Continuous Improvement Leaders;
- Define team performance objectives and professional development plans;
- Cultivate talent with expertise in Lean, Process Excellence, and Business Transformation;
- Foster a culture of continuous improvement throughout the organization.

Qualifications

Education
- Bachelor’s degree or higher in Business Administration, Operations Management, Industrial Engineering, Supply Chain Management, Engineering, or a related field;
- MBA, EMBA, or a Master’s degree in Engineering Management is preferred;
- Professional certifications such as Lean Six Sigma Black Belt or Master Black Belt are preferred.

Work Experience
- 20+ years of experience in operations management, process optimization, corporate transformation, or business management;
- 15+ years of experience in senior-level operational excellence, continuous improvement, or enterprise process management;
- Prior experience in roles such as VP of Operational Excellence, VP of Continuous Improvement, or VP of Business Transformation is preferred;
- Experience with operational improvement initiatives within large-scale enterprises, multi-business unit organizations, or cross-regional operations;
- Proven track record of successful enterprise-wide process restructuring, cost optimization, and operational transformation.

Core Competencies
- Operational Excellence;
- Continuous Improvement;
- Lean / Six Sigma;
- Business Process Optimization;
- Operational Performance Management;
- Business Transformation;
- Data-Driven Decision Making;
- Digital Transformation;
- Cost & Resource Optimization;
- Change Management;
- Cross-Functional Leadership;
- Executive Team Leadership.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
- Improvement rate of overall enterprise operational efficiency;
- Reduction rate of core business process cycle times;
- Rate of operational cost reduction;
- Improvement rate of employee and organizational productivity;
- Coverage rate of process standardization and automation;
- Improvement rate of product and service quality;
- Completion rate of operational improvement initiatives;
- Return on Investment (ROI) for improvement initiatives;
- Achievement rate of enterprise operational KPIs;
- Adoption and implementation rate of operational best practices.

